Third-party components and models
---------------------------------

KB-Whisper models (KBLab, National Library of Sweden / Kungliga biblioteket)
  https://huggingface.co/KBLab/kb-whisper-large (and -tiny, -base, -small, -medium)
  License: Apache License 2.0 (as stated on the Hugging Face model cards)
  The model weights are NOT included in this repository or in the release
  archives. They are downloaded by the user from Hugging Face on first use.
  Fine-tuned from OpenAI's Whisper checkpoints (openai/whisper-*, Apache-2.0).
  Citation: Vesterbacka, L., Rekathati, F., Kurtz, R., Sikora, J., Toftgård, A.
  (2025) Swedish Whispers; Leveraging a Massive Speech Corpus for Swedish Speech
  Recognition. Proc. Interspeech 2025, 758-762, doi:10.21437/Interspeech.2025-2646

Klang Pianissimo ("Snabb" in Prata) (KlangAI)
  https://huggingface.co/KlangAI/pianissimo-sv
  License: Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International (CC BY 4.0)
  https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/
  Prata uses KlangAI's official int8 ONNX export of this model,
  https://huggingface.co/KlangAI/pianissimo-sv-onnx (encoder-model.int8.onnx,
  decoder_joint-model.int8.onnx, vocab.txt), without modifications.
  The model files are NOT included in this repository or in the release
  archives. They are downloaded by the user from Hugging Face on first use.

ONNX Runtime (via the ort crate, https://github.com/pykeio/ort)
  https://github.com/microsoft/onnxruntime
  License: MIT (onnxruntime) / MIT OR Apache-2.0 (ort)
  Linked statically into builds with the "snabb" feature.

Hugging Face Candle (candle-core, candle-nn, candle-transformers)
  https://github.com/huggingface/candle
  License: Apache License 2.0 OR MIT
  crates/prata/src/main.rs is derived from candle's whisper example
  (candle-examples/examples/whisper), and crates/prata/src/melfilters*.bytes
  are the mel filter banks shipped with that example.

OpenAI Whisper (model architecture, decoding rules, mel filters)
  https://github.com/openai/whisper
  License: MIT (code); the openai/whisper-* model weights on Hugging Face are Apache-2.0

Other Rust crates (axum, tokio, serde, clap, hf-hub, tokenizers, …) are used
under their respective licenses (mostly MIT and/or Apache-2.0); see Cargo.lock.

The optional Python fallback (python/transcribe.py) uses PyTorch (BSD-3-Clause)
and Hugging Face Transformers (Apache-2.0), which are installed separately.

ffmpeg is required at runtime and is NOT bundled; it is installed separately by
the user (LGPL/GPL depending on the build).
